      "gap": "Source Theorem 2(ii) first part (p.87; proof p.88) -- if (psi0,F0) is a saddlepoint and the score set contains a nonzero multiple of -f0'/f0, then F0 minimizes I(F) over C -- is neither stated nor proved on the route. The handbook entry (parts lines 184-207, annex 347-386) is formulated only for a given minimizer F_* ('Let F_* in C minimize information') and gives the equivalence with the two saddlepoint inequalities under that premise; the converse direction (saddlepoint implies information minimizer) is missing as a written statement/proof (C005's minimax equality and C006's uniqueness discussion do not state it)."
