      "gap": "The source's Remark after Theorem 5 (p.91) states two variants that are not preserved: (a) if psi0' is uniformly continuous then -lambda_F'(0) = int psi0' dF for every F in C, hence V(psi0,F)=K(psi0,F)^{-1} and a K-saddlepoint is a V-saddlepoint when lambda_F(0)=0 on C; (b) for discontinuous psi0', -lambda_F'(0)=int psi0' dF still holds for F in C_1. The handbook (parts lines 225-235, annex 436-454) instead takes 'limsup_n a_psi(F_n) <= d_F' as an assumed premise and proves only the one-sided bound E_F psi^2/d_F^2 <= 1/alpha; neither the uniformly-continuous-derivative identity nor the C_1 identity is stated or proved, and the V-saddlepoint conclusion of the remark is not stated."
